      "side": 1,
      "message": "It looks like we are adding an extra permission check after checkAndNotifyCommonError has already checked permissions, and that check is only for this method (startTethering) but not for any of the other methods (including tether, which generally does the same thing as this method does).\n\nThat seems brittle - it seems better for all the permissions checks to be in one method that always performs the same checks. Per discussion, that might require passing in the TetheringRequest into checkAndNotifyCommonError. That would probably allow us to remove some of the parameters of that method, which are derived from the request (e.g., onlyAllowPrivileged).",
